<http://data.silknow.org/object/4293f041-40c3-367e-ab1a-850641e91eee/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Pair of sash borders of embroidered silk with silk and metal threads. With filling stitch is double darning on the diagonal, and other stitches of double running in a line, fishbone and needle-weaving. The metal thread embroidery is worked in fishbone stitch and double running in a line. Plate has been used to work in satin stitch and Tel Kirman (Turkish Plate Stitch) in isolated knots.\n\nWith a design of flower sprays and leaves. The spray on the left has a central stem with a single scrolled end from which spring smaller stems. The spray on the right consists of three stems joined at the bottom to a single stem with two scrolled ends. Underneath each spray is a small band of needle-weaving."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/4293f041-40c3-367e-ab1a-850641e91eee> .

<http://data.silknow.org/object/4293f041-40c3-367e-ab1a-850641e91eee/dimension/2>
